# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.

# https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# Optional: pull the graph live via `python -m src.cli pull` instead of a
# manual Roam export. Both required if you use it. Get the token from your
# graph's own settings in Roam (look for an "API tokens" section) — this
# tool has no way to generate one for you. See roam/api.py's module
# docstring: the wire format was sourced from a community client, not
# Roam's own docs, so `pull` is genuinely unverified until you run it once.
# ROAM_API_TOKEN=roam-graph-token-...
# ROAM_GRAPH_NAME=your-graph-name

# Model per stage. Defaults are in src/llm/openrouter.py — these override them.
# Run `python -m src.cli models` for the live catalog, cheapest first; run
# `python -m src.cli extract ... --dry-run` to price a run before making it.
#
# The tiering rationale is about VERIFIABILITY, not prestige:
#
#   extract  high-volume, mechanical, and independently checked — every triple
#            must quote its source block or it is dropped. A cheap model that
#            occasionally emits junk is affordable here, because the junk is
#            discarded rather than believed. Go cheap.
#
#   resolve  low-volume and unverifiable after the fact. A wrong merge welds two
#            entities' facts together and leaves no signal they were ever apart.
#            This is the stage to spend on. Do not cheapen it without running
#            `src.cli eval` against a gold set and reading `over_merge_rate`.
#
#   query    has to reason over a subgraph and cite it honestly. Cheap models
#            tend to answer from their own knowledge instead; `eval` reports
#            `hallucinated_citation_rate`, which is how you catch that.

# ROAMEX_MODEL_EXTRACT=qwen/qwen3.7-flash
# ROAMEX_MODEL_RESOLVE=google/gemini-3.6-flash
# ROAMEX_MODEL_QUERY=google/gemini-3.6-flash

# GOTCHA if you swap in a different reasoning-capable model: it can spend its
# whole max_tokens budget on reasoning and return empty content, which looks
# exactly like a broken extractor. Hit for real with qwen3.7-flash on extract
# (25/59 blocks failed) before openrouter.py started passing
# reasoning={"enabled": False} there. resolve/query keep reasoning ON —
# that's the judgment those stages are supposed to spend on — with a wider
# max_tokens (3072) instead. If a new model still comes back empty, raise
# max_tokens further before assuming the model or the prompt is broken.
